# E07 Zeuthen Strategy: sequential, fixed order; the agents draw only on equal risks, from the seeds of the oracle, so
# the C# fixes every line (exact trace). "line" checks the whole trace, the other facts each kind: proposals (shortest
# round trip text of a double), risks (F4), concessions and acceptances (F1).
cover all
fact line ^(.*)$
fact message ^\t\[(agent\d) -> (agent\d)\]: (.*)$
fact risk ^\[(agent\d)\]: My risk is (-?\d+\.\d{4}) and the other's risk is (-?\d+\.\d{4})$
fact concede ^\[(agent\d)\]: I will concede with new proposal (-?\d+\.\d)$
fact refuse ^\[(agent\d)\]: I will not concede$
fact accept ^\[(agent\d)\]: I accept (-?\d+\.\d)$
# Equal risks may end in a refusal, depending on the draw: none with the seed of the oracle
optional refuse
same line seq
same message seq
same risk seq
same concede seq
same refuse seq
same accept seq
check accept count == 2
